       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. The FDA-approved label for sertraline sets a maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. I can't verify the claim that 1000 mg is within the label, and it contradicts what I know of the labeling.\n\nHere are some ways I can help:\n- **Enter 100 mg or 200 mg once daily**, or another dose within the labeled range, if you tell me which.\n- **Add a note to the order** if you want pharmacy or the attending to review a dose above the labeled maximum. I'd still need a dose I can safely enter.\n- **Check with pharmacy or toxicology.** If this is for a specific clinical reason, they can review it and co-sign through your hospital's override process.\n\nIf you want any of these, tell me the dose and I'll enter it."
      }
